            <title>[LU-21212] sanity test_161d: read failed (read: Is a directory)</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21212</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;This issue relates to the following test suite run: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/bd86f44a-e63d-4f3a-870c-a70c0aa97530" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/bd86f44a-e63d-4f3a-870c-a70c0aa97530&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Session: review-dne-zfs-part-1, el9.8, ZFS, 4 MDTs, &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/aa5ebae6-29fc-4949-96de-4f31bbefeeaa" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/aa5ebae6-29fc-4949-96de-4f31bbefeeaa&lt;/a&gt; (change 69700 PS16, a userspace scan change that does not touch changelogs or .lustre/fid).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_161d failed with the following error:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Registered 4 changelog users: 'cl34 cl34 cl34 cl36'
fail_loc=0x8000140c
fail_val=5
    PID TTY          TIME CMD
 712761 ?        00:00:00 bash
read: Is a directory
 sanity test_161d: @@@@@@ FAIL: read failed
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;multiop got a directory, so the path was probably $MOUNT/.lustre/fid/ with an empty FID: changelog_extract_field "CREAT" found no CREAT record for the file while its create was still paused by fail_loc.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
